WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.780
National home prices fell 20.5% from their 2022 peak, hitting Canadian bank mortgage books hardest. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 220. We'll check the indexes, then how to confirm money is rotating into financials, and a simulated bank of Montreal hold. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.960
advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:44.760
money to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,541, down 0.5%. While the TSX composite closed

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:58.820
at 35,801, up 0.5%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 25,164, down 1.1%, up 8.30% year-to-date,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:05.220
and up 12.47% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16th, 2026.

00:01:06.452 --> 00:01:11.092
Housing dependent sectors and financials are under pressure, and the next federal reserve

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:16.312
and bank of Canada decisions remain the frame that rate-sensitive names are reprising against.

00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:23.172
AI infrastructure names saw mixed flows as local opposition to data centers reach 71%,

00:01:23.512 --> 00:01:26.812
higher than opposition to nuclear plants in the same Gallup poll.

00:01:26.812 --> 00:01:33.372
energy producers lagged as oil prices eased from recent highs. About 14 days ago we

00:01:33.372 --> 00:01:38.552
picked GM on earning surprise valuation support after sector rotation and it

00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:44.292
closed down 1.18%. Showing how a single name can lag even when the broader setup

00:01:44.292 --> 00:01:49.332
looks stable. Sector rotation confirmation asks whether money is already moving

00:01:49.332 --> 00:01:54.352
into a whole group before you size any single name inside it. An unusual whale

00:01:54.352 --> 00:01:59.292
Bill's carried the BMO capital markets breakdown that makes that test worth running on Canadian

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:00.212
banks right now.

00:02:00.872 --> 00:02:06.072
I have no financial relationship with wealth simple, interactive brokers, unusual whales,

00:02:06.352 --> 00:02:07.152
or the Motley Fool.

00:02:07.832 --> 00:02:13.072
BMO capital markets shows the housing correction has hit recent buyers hardest, while leaving

00:02:13.072 --> 00:02:18.772
almost half the country comparatively unscathed, which means mortgage book pain is uneven rather

00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:19.412
than national.

00:02:19.412 --> 00:02:26.012
The drop sits close to the 26% decline the United States saw during the 2008 housing crash.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:31.052
After prices here surged roughly 50% in the final two years before the peak.

00:02:31.672 --> 00:02:37.152
The decline is concentrated in two provinces, so a cheap looking bank yield and a quiet ticker

00:02:37.152 --> 00:02:41.032
is not automatically a bargain if that book is tied to those two markets.

00:02:42.052 --> 00:02:47.292
Investor-owned condos, particularly small units in Toronto and Vancouver, are another pressure

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:47.612
point.

00:02:47.612 --> 00:02:53.152
and the Bank of Canada has flagged a large stock of unsold small condominiums in both cities.

00:02:53.652 --> 00:02:56.352
A slowdown in immigration has added to the drag,

00:02:56.872 --> 00:03:01.492
removing a key source of housing demand just as a wave of rental supply comes to market.

00:03:02.052 --> 00:03:08.112
You implement the filter by pulling sector ETF flows for financials on wealth simple or interactive brokers,

00:03:08.552 --> 00:03:16.772
then comparing the 20-day average volume in the Canadian financials ETF, ticker XFN against the broader TSX.

00:03:16.772 --> 00:03:23.532
When financials volume exceeds its average while the broader index lags, the setup meets the rotation test.

00:03:23.892 --> 00:03:30.172
The same check fails when individual bank names weaken on low volume, even if the sector headline looks stable.

00:03:30.832 --> 00:03:34.032
It is like checking the mall parking lot before you lease a storefront.

00:03:34.552 --> 00:03:43.072
An empty lot means even a cheap unit will not get walk-in traffic, and a bank yield works the same way if the whole financials group is not attracting money.

00:03:43.072 --> 00:03:49.152
That filter has kept dividend names out of weak rotation environments in past cycles where single

00:03:49.152 --> 00:03:55.132
name yield support proved insufficient. Remember, confirm the sector is attracting money before you buy

00:03:55.132 --> 00:04:02.546
the cheapest name in it. Bank of Montreal, ticker BMO on the TSX, is today's simulated weekly hold,

00:04:03.006 --> 00:04:08.446
evaluation entry on housing correction exposure with sector rotation confirmation already in place,

00:04:08.446 --> 00:04:12.526
case, and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:18.846
You see the shares sitting below the 50-session average close on daily bars, while XFN volume

00:04:18.846 --> 00:04:24.166
already exceeds its 20-day average. Do you treat that as a value trap or as a confirmed

00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:29.466
rotation into the group? Here's how I'd think about it. The last dividend name hold went

00:04:29.466 --> 00:04:34.046
on without that sector flow check, while the name was already showing relative weakness,

00:04:34.046 --> 00:04:39.166
And that is why this bank of Montreal entry only activates when broader money is already

00:04:39.166 --> 00:04:40.966
moving into financials.

00:04:41.306 --> 00:04:46.306
Catalysts is that BMO's own research desk is the source of the housing warning, and

00:04:46.306 --> 00:04:51.146
the bank is also a lender on that same book, so the position is a direct read on whether

00:04:51.146 --> 00:04:52.426
damage stays contained.

00:04:53.086 --> 00:04:59.066
The approach also uses the two province concentration, which narrows which banks are most exposed and

00:04:59.066 --> 00:05:02.146
keeps this from being a blanket bet on every Canadian lender.

00:05:02.146 --> 00:05:09.606
And 8% stop loss sits below entry and caps the loss at $80 on the $1,000 position, if

00:05:09.606 --> 00:05:11.746
the low of any session reaches that level.

00:05:12.626 --> 00:05:14.686
Invalidation is not a second price line.

00:05:15.226 --> 00:05:20.626
If Bank of Montreal's next quarterly credit loss provision rises more than 15% year over

00:05:20.626 --> 00:05:25.486
year, the contained damage thesis is broken before the stop even has to do the work.

00:05:26.026 --> 00:05:30.206
Target is plus 2% to plus 5% over a five session hold.

00:05:30.206 --> 00:05:35.926
Confidence is medium because sector rotation, confirmation, and valuation support are aligned.

00:05:36.426 --> 00:05:39.346
Yet the single-name credit-loss catalyst remains pending.

00:05:39.946 --> 00:05:44.746
It enters at the next session's open under the published weekly hold rules and is judged

00:05:44.746 --> 00:05:49.186
against the NASDAQ over those five sessions, with no discretionary exit.

00:05:49.806 --> 00:05:55.666
Open your brokerage platform, pull up BMO on the TSX, and check whether its 20-day average

00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:58.986
volume sits above or below the broader financial's ETF.

00:05:58.986 --> 00:06:01.546
F. Note the result in under five minutes.

00:06:02.206 --> 00:06:07.226
Cenevis Energy, ticker CVE on the TSX, was the last weekly hold.

00:06:07.686 --> 00:06:13.646
A dividend income entry on elevated oil prices and a 26 year payout growth streak, simulated

00:06:13.646 --> 00:06:17.366
from the Tuesday open through the Monday close across five sessions.

00:06:17.846 --> 00:06:24.106
We simulated buying it at $46.12, and exiting at $42.95.

00:06:24.106 --> 00:06:31.146
cents, a loss of 6.87%, or $68.73 on the $1,000 position.

00:06:31.846 --> 00:06:38.766
The NASDAQ lost 4.27% over the same window, so alpha was negative 2.60%.

00:06:38.766 --> 00:06:42.166
A loss against the benchmark, not just a red P&amp;L.

00:06:42.686 --> 00:06:48.266
Stated confidence was medium, the stated invalidation was a quarterly dividend coverage ratio falling

00:06:48.266 --> 00:06:52.286
below 1.1 times on the November call, and it never mattered.

00:06:52.286 --> 00:06:57.766
The 8% stop was not reached either, so the hold ran the full five sessions and still

00:06:57.766 --> 00:07:00.446
finished behind both the entry and the NASDAQ.

00:07:00.866 --> 00:07:05.466
Medium correctly reflected mixed oil price support against broader rotation pressure,

00:07:05.886 --> 00:07:09.286
and the invalidation never had a chance to fire inside that window.

00:07:09.846 --> 00:07:13.026
This didn't work, and the adjustment is the one already on the card.

00:07:13.586 --> 00:07:18.406
Require sector rotation confirmation before entering any dividend name already showing

00:07:18.406 --> 00:07:19.366
relative weakness.

